1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:20,687
Inez took the lead at the first turn. Cassius took it from her at the
second. I took it from both of them at the third, because a nigga can
appreciate romance without letting it control the standings. The
Lamborghini climbed out of the harbor with the sea flashing behind us.
Flags snapped above the road.

2
00:00:20,937 --> 00:00:41,880
People crowded the balconies, shouting our names as we passed. Mine
came loudest, but I could hear Inez's too, and Cassius's, and once
Nero's from a man who saw the silver car and forgot which generation
had come back to race. The engine settled beneath my hands. No
passenger this time.

3
00:00:42,130 --> 00:01:04,187
Shawna's seat held only the blue handkerchief she had given me before
the boat race. I had folded it carefully and tucked one corner beneath
the belt so it wouldn't fly away. Nigga, a man can drive alone without
leaving everybody behind. The first miles ran through vineyards. Low
stone walls. Green hills. Sun on the hood.

4
00:01:04,437 --> 00:01:26,898
Sabine pressed hard on my left, her yellow car taking the turns with
clean, patient precision. Adrian came up behind her. Inez stayed close
to Cassius, then split away on the long bend and passed him with a
laugh over the race channel. Try to finish that sentence before next
year, she told him. Nigga, I'm busy. So am I.

5
00:01:27,148 --> 00:01:49,712
I smiled and took the next turn faster. At the old fort, the road
narrowed beneath an archway. I went through first. Sabine followed.
Behind her, a black car came out of a side entrance wearing no number
and no interest in the rules. Here we fucking go. It struck Adrian's
rear corner. His car slid toward the wall.

6
00:01:49,962 --> 00:02:15,056
He caught it, swore and kept moving. Two more black cars emerged
behind the first, engines roaring, windows dark. The duke's final
team. Unmarked cars at the fort, I said into the channel. Odette
answered immediately. We see them. Knox's voice followed. Keep your
road, Captain. Nigga, I planned to. The first black car pushed between
Sabine and me.

7
00:02:15,306 --> 00:02:37,217
Its driver wore a helmet with a gold stripe. He looked over as he came
alongside, and I could see the smile behind his visor. That nigga had
been hired to be a problem. I could see him rehearsing the moment in
his own head: the famous captain frightened, the crowd quiet, the duke
nodding like he'd bought himself the correct nigga.

8
00:02:37,467 --> 00:03:00,891
"You see him?" Inez asked over the channel. "I see the nigga." "He's
looking at you." "Nigga should look where he's going." Cassius
laughed. "You about to change where that nigga's going, aren't you?"
"Depends how hard he asks." Sabine's voice joined us. "These niggas do
this every race?" "Every beautiful race," Inez said. I hoped he had
been paid in advance.

9
00:03:01,141 --> 00:03:22,825
He moved toward me. I let him come. Then I braked just enough to let
his front cross mine and turned behind him before he could correct. He
struck the wall with his rear quarter, bounced back onto the road and
found Sabine already gone past him on the other side. Nigga, she said
over the channel, that was rude. You talking to me? No.

10
00:03:23,075 --> 00:03:46,938
I'm learning your punctuation. I laughed and accelerated. The black
car recovered. Came again. Behind us, Inez and Cassius boxed the
second attacker away from Adrian, keeping him from being forced toward
the drop. They didn't touch the black car. They gave its driver no
clean space to become violent without losing his own road. He lost it
anyway.

11
00:03:47,188 --> 00:04:08,169
The car struck a low wall, spun and stopped across a gravel turnout.
Its driver climbed out with both hands raised when Odette's pursuit
car reached him. One down. Two still coming. The interior road ran
through a pine forest. Sunlight broke in strips across the windshield.
My speed climbed.

12
00:04:08,419 --> 00:04:29,910
The gold-striped driver stayed with me, closer now, his car powerful
enough to make arrogance feel supported. He showed me a gun through
the side window. Nigga, that was his introduction. I answered with my
siren. The blue lights flashed through the trees. He fired. The shot
struck the road ahead of my front wheel.

13
00:04:30,160 --> 00:04:51,157
I moved, felt the car slide, brought it back and saw the narrow
service lane opening on my right. I took it. The black car followed.
The lane led through an old stone winery courtyard and rejoined the
race road above the next bend. Barrels lined one wall. A tractor stood
beneath a canopy.

14
00:04:51,407 --> 00:05:13,242
Two workers jumped aside as I came through, my siren giving them the
only explanation they needed. The black car entered too fast. Its side
struck the tractor's rear wheel. The machine spun across the courtyard
in a long ugly scrape and stopped against a stack of empty barrels.
The driver tried to reverse. Couldn't.

15
00:05:13,492 --> 00:05:31,959
His gun hand came up again as I turned through the far gate. I fired
once from my window. His windshield cracked in front of him. He ducked
and dropped the gun. I kept going. Nigga, stay parked. At the
rejoining road, Sabine flashed past. Then Adrian.

16
00:05:32,209 --> 00:05:55,235
I came in behind them, still third, with Inez and Cassius close enough
to make the race feel like a promise instead of a procession. The last
unmarked car waited at the gorge. Not on the road. Across it. Beyond
the car, the old stone bridge had been blocked by two service trucks.
Men stood beside them with weapons visible.

17
00:05:55,485 --> 00:06:19,003
The race officials on the near side waved frantically, trying to stop
us before the road narrowed. Sabine braked. Adrian pulled beside her.
I stopped behind them. The other drivers arrived and got out. For the
first time all day, the engines sounded small against the space around
us. Across the gorge, the palace road climbed toward the finish.

18
00:06:19,253 --> 00:06:42,765
We could see its flags above the trees. The duke had put a wall
between the race and the result. A man in a green coat stepped onto
the bridge with a loudspeaker. By order of His Grace, the Grand Prix
is suspended. Nigga, I said, he losing so hard he canceled geography.
Inez came beside me. There's an old bridge below. I looked down.

19
00:06:43,015 --> 00:07:08,054
A narrow stone crossing lay farther along the gorge, reached by a
steep track cut into the hillside. It had been built for carts, not
modern race cars. Ivy covered one side. A fallen branch lay across its
far end. Cassius followed my eyes. No. Yes, I said. Aiden. Nigga, you
keep saying my name like it means stop. Sabine looked at the track.

20
00:07:08,304 --> 00:07:33,236
Then at my car. You're serious. Very attractive too. We got a list
going. Adrian laughed once, sharp and disbelieving. The man on the
bridge lifted the loudspeaker again. All drivers will remain where
they are. I held up my badge. Captain Aiden. All niggas with borrowed
guns can put them down. He stared. I got back in my car. The others
followed.

21
00:07:33,486 --> 00:07:58,528
We took the old track together. Slow at first. The slope was rough,
the edge close. I kept the Lamborghini steady while stones cracked
beneath the tires and dust rose around the hood. Above us, the duke's
men shouted. One fired into the air. Odette's officers reached the
main bridge behind them and answered with commands that sounded much
more practiced than mine.

22
00:07:58,778 --> 00:08:21,781
We kept descending. At the old crossing, I stopped. The stone bridge
was narrower than it had looked from above. My mirrors had inches on
either side. The branch at the far end was larger too, a whole fallen
limb across the exit. I got out. Tank's voice came through the
channel. Nigga, why you out of the car? Moving a tree.

23
00:08:22,031 --> 00:08:44,710
Of course you are. I climbed onto the bridge and crossed on foot. The
gorge opened beneath me, water bright far below. The old stones felt
solid under my shoes. At the far end I caught the branch in both hands
and pulled. It moved a little. Sabine got out behind me. Then Adrian.
Then Cassius and Inez.

24
00:08:44,960 --> 00:09:08,277
We lifted it together and rolled it off the road. No speech. No
photograph arranged afterward. Five drivers who wanted to beat one
another cleared the same bridge because none of us had come to let
Aurelio choose where we stopped. I looked at them. Niggas ready? Inez
grinned. Move your beautiful car. I did. The Lamborghini crossed
first.

25
00:09:08,527 --> 00:09:32,299
Slowly enough that every stone had time to judge us. Then Sabine.
Adrian. Inez. Cassius last. As his silver car reached the far end, the
duke's men appeared on the upper path. Gunfire struck the slope above
us. We drove. The track climbed toward the palace road in a series of
tight turns. Dirt flew. Engines roared.

26
00:09:32,549 --> 00:09:55,328
I hit the paved road first and let the Lamborghini stretch beneath me,
all the careful restraint of the gorge releasing at once. Ahead stood
the final hill. Beyond it, the finish. The duke had one more idea. A
helicopter rose from the palace grounds and hovered above the road,
low enough for its wind to tear leaves from the trees.

27
00:09:55,578 --> 00:10:19,873
A man leaned out with a weapon aimed toward the cars. Nigga had
upgraded the weather. I saw the first flashes and drove beneath the
line of trees. Branches struck the roof. The helicopter followed, its
shadow racing beside me. Behind, the others spread out, making
themselves harder to trap in one straight line. I called the thunder.
One short burst.

28
00:10:20,123 --> 00:10:45,116
Blue light ran through the wheel, into the dash, beneath the hood. The
Lamborghini surged. The road came toward me faster, the car answering
like a living thing that had waited for the last demand. I passed
beneath the helicopter before the gunman could follow my movement.
Ahead, a low stone ramp rose beside the road, part of an old loading
terrace. I took it.

29
00:10:45,366 --> 00:11:10,182
The car lifted. For a second the palace gates filled the windshield.
Then the Lamborghini landed beyond the line of concrete barriers the
duke had placed across the entrance, tires striking the courtyard road
with a sound that made every guard turn. Blue lights flashed over
white marble. My siren filled the palace. Nigga, the finish line had
been trying to hide in a fortress.

30
00:11:10,432 --> 00:11:30,774
I brought the whole police department to its door. The official race
arch still stood in the courtyard, ribbons moving in the helicopter's
wind. Lord Orlan waited beneath it with the seventh key in a velvet
case, pale and sweating. The duke stood on the palace steps beside the
stranger in the dark uniform.

31
00:11:31,024 --> 00:11:55,081
Shawna was at the far side of the courtyard with my people. I saw her
before I stopped. Just like she asked. I crossed the line first. The
bells began ringing. The crowd outside the gates heard them and
roared. Inez came through the opening the guards had finally cleared.
Cassius followed. Sabine. Adrian. All five of us reached the courtyard
alive.

32
00:11:55,331 --> 00:12:17,495
I sat in the car for one breath while the thunder's cost rolled
through my shoulders. One breath. Then I opened the door and stood.
Shawna ran to me. I caught her with both arms, lifted her and kissed
her in front of the palace, the drivers, the guards, the duke and
every camera that had followed me across a month of his bad decisions.

33
00:12:17,745 --> 00:12:41,648
Nigga, she whispered against my mouth, you did it. I looked over her
shoulder at Aurelio. His face had gone empty. No smile. No threat.
Nothing left to arrange between himself and what everybody had seen. I
put Shawna gently on her feet. Then I walked toward the seventh key.
Lord Orlan held it out. The duke drew a gun. Nobody moves, he said.

34
00:12:41,898 --> 00:12:45,524
Nigga, the race was over. Now he wanted to meet me.
